      {
        "id": 69348,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-31T16:37:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This thread, the sympathetic villains thread and the who would win thread have me thinking about Iron Legacy redeemed, and what he would be like then.</p><p>I'd add some cards to show he's not clean cut anymore, he'd probably be more offensive than before, and I'd leave him with some anger.</p><p>I'd love a base power of damage, maybe a couple of targets low damage, and then a card where he'd get a boost that would last for some time, but fade or explode or something. &nbsp;Maybe a card you play that puts a card or two from his deck under it, then takes one out from under at the start of his turn, let him add any targets he destroys under it. &nbsp;Boost damage by 1 for each card underneath. &nbsp;As long as there are targets to destroy he could keep his damage up, but if he can't beat anyone down, then it fades each round. &nbsp;A card that would let him grab a villain target with 5 or less max HP and use it as a weapon to hit other villains would be awesome, have it lose HP each time he uses it. &nbsp;Stuff that lets him go on sick little rampages through minion hordes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:47:54.453Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
