      {
        "id": 69350,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-31T19:21:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p>Place this card next to a villain target with HP of 5 or less.&nbsp;</p><p>At the beginning of your turn deal that villain target 1 melee damage and then deal X damage to another target, where X = the first target's HP.&nbsp;</p></blockquote><p>I forgot to add in using that target as a shield, where you could redirect any damage dealt to a hero target to that card instead.</p><p>It would be very dark-legacy to use an enemy as a weapon or a shield. &nbsp;Or it could be a totally new hero who brawls and tanks with less damage than Haka and less tanking than Legacy, and less fixing than the fixer.</p><p>I'd alter it a bit:</p><blockquote><p>Take a villain target with 5 or less max hp and put it in your play area, as long as it is in your play area ignore its text, put this card next to it.</p><p>You may redirect damage dealt to a hero target to the target attached to this card. &nbsp;</p><p>Power: &nbsp;Deal one villain target the HP of the card attached to this card, then deal the attached card one damage. &nbsp;If this power is not used during your turn destroy this card.</p><span>If the target attached to this card is destroyed, destroy this card. &nbsp;If this card is destroyed return the target to the villain play area with it's current HP.</span></blockquote><p>That is probably way too much text, someone better at doing rules could probably condense it and make sense.</p><p>Pair it with a card like:</p><blockquote><p>The first time (name) would take damage each turn you may redirect one point of damage to an ally.</p></blockquote><p>Call it keep your friends close, and the one above keep your enemies closer.</p><p>I'm going to have to work on some more cards for this, because an antihero Brawler/tank would be awesome.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:47:54.635Z",
